                    stock-preseeded-40k-1home started 2026-11-01 04:17 UTC at harness 477013a and was stopped at 12:01 with 23,973 credentials witnessed in its preseed, before its measured window opened. Per 2,000 credentials, the issuer's own stamps stayed flat throughout: anchored to witnessed 0.11 to 0.24 s and witnessed to published 0.48 to 0.53 s, from the first credential to the 22,000th. Yet the fill rate, 4 in flight, fell from 1.40 to 1.52 a second over the first 8,000 to 0.85 to 1.03 between 12,000 and 20,000 and 0.31 past 22,000, where accepted to anchored jumped from about 1.9 s to 11.8 s. At 12:00 one of the three witness processes held 8.4 GB resident and ran at 53% of a core, against 156 MB and 85 MB for the other two, and the host had 4 GB of 23 GB left. So the growth this fill found is outside imbu's stages and most likely in the witnesses as one KEL grows past 20,000 events, which heti-consumer-kel says it did not change (witness#43's, witness-side serving); this host has no profiler, so it is not proven. Stopped rather than finished because at 0.3 a second and falling the remaining 16,000 would take over 15 hours with the host near swap, and the PM's order is to rerun target 3 first. The preseed's timeline is kept as target 2's evidence for 10,000 to 24,000, gzipped with what it was cut from. The measured window, 0.1 a second for 30 minutes with the issuer killed at 900 s, runs instead on the first run's own scenario, stock-preseeded-1home at 10,000, after target 3, so restart time at stock compares at equal stock with the first run's 10.8 s. Rejected restarting the 40,000 fill: it would hit the same wall. Rejected a 20,000 preseed: the slowdown begins near there, so its window would measure the witness, not the issuer's stock. Tradeoff: no restart time is measured above 10,000.
            Target 3 is rerun on heti 980ee85, heti-consumer-kel, overriding the heti imbu 2c3b072 pins, and only target 3 = decision:
              nid: 53kz99e2
              why: >-
                The rerun's office day at three homes (2026-10-31 11:25 to 20:12 UTC, harness 58df2a9, heti 1ae3590) held issuance flat but verified only 13 of its 100 sampled credentials: from about credential 1,111 heti's verifier, and from 2,121 its holder, timed out resolving the issuer, because heti's lockbox fetched and replayed the issuer's whole KEL from a witness inside a 10 s deadline (lockbox._resolve_other), and the holder answered e.state.pending.observation.r with the issuer's key state up to 6,605 s old. The PM launched heti-consumer-kel for it, which landed on heti utah/next as 980ee85 (heti @557x8ypw): a refresh of an issuer whose KEL heti already holds replays only the new events, and a first resolution too long for one deadline raises e.state.pending.replay.r with its progress kept. The PM's instruction (2026-10-31) is to repin and rerun target 3 before the report lands. imbu 2c3b072 pins heti 1ae3590, and imbu is not this item's to change before the summit, so keri-bench overrides the heti requirement to 980ee85 with uv's override-dependencies, which makes the issuer's imbu run on it too; 980ee85 descends from 1ae3590, and the override is the whole of the difference. Only office-day-3homes is rerun, in a worktree of its own (bench-targets-2-heti), so targets 1, 2, 4 and 5 stay on the one stack imbu pins and every number in their before-and-after has one heti beneath it; the rerun's office day also gives target 1's three-home office-day verdict a second reading, reported beside the first and not in place of it. Not changed by 980ee85: every refresh still downloads the whole KEL from each witness it asks (witness-side serving is witness#43's), so if target 3 still fails past some stock, that is where to look. Rejected repinning everything to 980ee85 and rerunning targets 1, 2, 4 and 5: the stack they would measure is not the one imbu pins, and the issuer path heti-consumer-kel changes is the consumer's, not issuance's. Tradeoff: the report carries two heti pins, and says which number came from which.
              children:
                bench-revocation reruns target 3 on heti 5623e2e, heti-observer-gap, with everything else as 53kz99e2's run = decision:
                  nid: 8wsdm5fz
                  why: >-
                    The rerun of target 3 on heti 980ee85 (results/targets-2026-10-rerun-heti, 2026-11-01) recognised 94 of 96 revocations within 30 minutes, and the other 2 never: heti's Observer held each one's issued chain with its registry gapped to the end of the run, while the Registrar held the revoked one (keri-bench tick ~52qg). heti-observer-gap found that the Observer kept retryably refused heads in an in-memory queue capped at 64 and dropped what did not fit, and fixed it on heti utah/next at 5623e2e (heti @3prxc795): refused heads persist in the Observer's store and are retried until they verify or fail for good, and passing the cap resubscribes instead of dropping. The PM's brief for bench-revocation (2026-11-02) asks for target 3 rerun exactly as before on that heti. So the override that 53kz99e2 put over imbu 2c3b072's heti pin moves from 980ee85 to 5623e2e, which descends from it, and nothing else changes: imbu stays at 2c3b072 though the brief allows later, so the before-and-after has one difference beneath it; the scenario is office-day-3homes unchanged, every 101st credential through revocation, on the same host with the same harness, a fresh calibration first and witness and issuer memory sampled every 5 minutes as in that run. The verdict is pass or fail against 1,800 s over the sampled revocations, with the distribution, and whether any registry the verifier met is still gapped at the Observer when the run ends, read from the Observer's and Registrar's stores as the 980ee85 run was. Rejected moving imbu to a later utah/next at the same time: two changes would leave a difference unattributable. Tradeoff: one run, so the two misses' absence is evidence about a 2% rate on a sample of about 100, not proof.
